// The system tasks and functions, and the built-in methods, that SIR names in the first operand of
// syscall and builtin (docs/notes/sir-v1-proposal.md, "The schema"; approved 2026-11-08). The one
// place that says which names SIR has: sir::sysTask and sir::builtinMethod read it, the verifier and
// the VM use them.
//   KIRIMASIM_SIR_SYSTASK_KIND(Kind)                       a kind of system task
//   KIRIMASIM_SIR_SYSTASK(Kind, "$name", minOperands, formatStart)
//       a name of that kind; minOperands counts the name itself and is what the VM's handler reads
//       by position; formatStart is the operand where a format and its values start, 0 for none
//   KIRIMASIM_SIR_METHOD(Kind, "name")                     a built-in method
// Several names share a kind: the b, o and h forms of the display tasks differ only in their radix,
// and the $dist_ functions share one handler (each with its own minimum: uniform, normal and erlang
// read two arguments after the seed).

KIRIMASIM_SIR_SYSTASK_KIND(Display)
KIRIMASIM_SIR_SYSTASK_KIND(Write)
